00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:04.870 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  we want baber and mid suffolk to  continue to be places that people are  proud to call home  and we have created our joint local plan  as a blueprint to help provide bright  and healthy futures for our districts  we have a legal responsibility to  deliver this plan  setting out where new homes will be  built in our districts and how we will  meet government housing requirements  up to 2037. affordable housing is a key  component of the plan  so that everyone can afford to live and  work in the places where they grew up  but it's not just homes that are being  built it is communities  the plan also details important  infrastructure  such as schools highways improvements  gp surgeries and other community  facilities  to ensure that we meet the needs of our  growing and changing population  sustainable transport options as well as  biodiversity  and environmental measures have been  promoted in the plan  as part of our council's ongoing  commitment to addressing climate change  our plan will also help us regenerate  key market towns  such as hadley sudbury stone market  needham market and i at a time  when economic growth and employment  opportunities  are needed more than ever i've been a  councillor for almost 30 years  and believe that the hard work and  commitment of officers together with the  council of working group  has produced a plan of the highest  quality backed up with more evidence  than i have ever seen support a plan  baba is a fantastic place to live work  and visit  and our plan aims to protect our  wonderful landscape  and areas of outstanding natural beauty  with its rich heritage  there's much to be proud of in our  district  the plan is set to preserve and enhance  what makes mid-suffolk special whilst  managing growth in our communities  for years to come how  and where development takes place is  incredibly important to us all  thank you to everyone who participated  in our previous public consultations  your views have helped shape our  district's future and ensured that our  plan includes the right options  and priorities our councils have now  submitted our plan  along with the final representations  received to an independent planning  inspector  appointed by government for examination  before  our joint local plan can be adopted  please visit our website for further  information  and updates as the plan progresses  you

